      ],
      "extract": "One of the most interesting topological solitons, which appear in the scalar field theories in 3+1 dimensional space-time, are so-called \\\"Hopfions\\\" [@Faddeev-Hopf; @Faddeev:1996zj]. These stable field configurations, whose topology is defined by the first Hopf map ${S}^3 \\mapsto {S}^2$, provide a first, and the best known example of knot solitons in field theory. It was suggested later that stable knotted vortex",
      "extractCut": true
    },
    {
