          "term": "phi times",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "The Lagrangian density of the Faddeev-Skyrme model in (3+1)-dimensional flat space can be written in terms of the real triplet of scalar fields $\\vec\\phi=(\\phi_1,\\phi_2,\\phi_3)$ as [@Faddeev-Hopf; @Faddeev:1996zj] $$\\label{lagr} \\ensuremath{\\mathcal{L}}=\\int d^3 x\\left[c_2\\partial_\\mu \\vec\\phi\\cdot\\partial^\\mu \\vec\\phi - \\frac{c_4}{2}\\left(\\partial_\\mu \\vec\\phi\\times\\partial_\\nu \\vec\\phi\\right)^2 - V(\\phi)\\right]$$",
      "extractCut": true
    },
