      "extract": "The peculiarity of the Faddeev-Skyrme model is that the Hopf index is not a winding number, the boundary conditions are identical for configurations in all topological sectors. As usual, the energy minimization scheme needs an appropriate initial configuration in a given sector. The most effective approach here is related with the generalization of the rational map approximation, suggested by Sutcliffe",
      "extractCut": true
